{
  "answer": "The sky appears blue because of a phenomenon called Rayleigh scattering. When sunlight enters Earth's atmosphere, it encounters molecules of nitrogen and oxygen. Sunlight is made up of different colors, each with a different wavelength. Blue light has a shorter wavelength and is scattered more by these molecules, making the sky appear blue to an observer on Earth."
}

